            <div xml:id="d419">

                <pb facs="0548" n="460" sameAs="frus:frus1933v05/pg460"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">837.00/4082: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Cuba</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Welles</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-10-01T18:00:00-05:00">October 1, 1933—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 7:20 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>328. Martínez Saenz informed me this morning that the Uruguayan Consul here had
                    advised him earlier that he and the Chargé d’Affaires <pb facs="0549" n="461"
                        xml:id="pg461"/> of Chile and the Chargé d’Affaires of Mexico were offering
                    to mediate between the government and the opposition to help find a solution of
                    the present problem. He told me he had replied that he felt that no effort of
                    this kind would be successful unless I agreed to join and requested my opinion.
                    He also said he was confident Grau San Martín would not accept the offer.</p>
                <p>I replied that I would of course welcome any effort by the diplomatic
                    representatives of American Republics to help the Cubans reach a solution of
                    their difficulties and that I could only express my sincere hope for their
                    success; that I appreciated his reference to myself but that I felt it would be
                    advisable not to raise the question of my participation.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
